# REFERENCE ONLY — hyprlock uses PAM.
#
# On many systems hyprlock uses /etc/pam.d/hyprlock if present, otherwise
# falls back toward login/system-auth. Inspect the image:
#   cat /etc/pam.d/hyprlock 2>/dev/null || echo "no hyprlock pam file"
#
# If hyprlock includes system-auth, enabling pam_duress there covers unlock.
# If hyprlock has a standalone stack, insert the same sufficient line after
# pam_unix (see system-auth.snippet).
#
# Test plan after enable:
#   1. hyprlock with normal password → unlock, no wipe
#   2. hyprlock with signed duress password → unlock + scripts run
